by nicolas-grekas at 2026-08-15T13:05:21Z

Thanks @Bellangelo, and sorry the promised review never came; I took it now. The design was better than it first looks: wrapping only engages on an interactive terminal via `stream_isatty`, so piped output, generated docs and every descriptor test fixture stay byte-for-byte unchanged. That decision is what made the rest reviewable, and it is kept.

What I changed, rebasing on 8.2 and squashing with your authorship:

* the rebase was a real merge: `TextDescriptor` gained the `[deprecated]`/`[hidden]` option rendering and a `Helper::width()` multibyte fix on 8.2 meanwhile, so your two-layout wrapping is now applied on top of those method bodies rather than replacing them;
* the wrap engine moved from `wordwrap()` to the component's own `OutputWrapper`. `wordwrap()` counts bytes and formatter tags, so UTF-8 descriptions wrapped early, a long token could be split mid-multibyte-character, and the invisible `<comment>` markup around defaults consumed visible columns. `OutputWrapper` measures visible width and never breaks inside a tag; three regression tests pin the tag, multibyte and non-tty behaviours;
* one genuine bug this uncovered: with the non-tty `PHP_INT_MAX` width flowing into the wrapper, the PCRE quantifier it builds exceeds the 65535 limit and `preg_replace()` returns null, which silently erased descriptions. The wrap is now skipped above 65535 columns, with a comment saying why.

Console is green at 1807 tests (tty group excluded locally), the descriptor suite at 155, and restoring the base descriptor fails 7 of the wrapping tests.
